# CHANGELOG.md is append-at-the-top and every branch adds an entry, so any two
# concurrent branches conflict there by construction. On 2026-10-31 that
# happened five times in one evening across three agents working in parallel
# (Claude, Cursor, Codex), twice leaving unresolved <<<<<<< markers committed
# to main, and repeatedly re-blocking pull requests that were otherwise green.
#
# `merge=union` takes BOTH sides instead of stopping. That is exactly the
# resolution a human performs every time here — the entries are independent
# prose and keeping both is always correct — so automating it loses no
# information and no judgement.
#
# union is a merge driver built into git itself, not a custom one needing
# local config, so it applies to GitHub's server-side merges as well as to
# `git merge` on a developer's machine. A custom driver would not.
#
# Deliberately scoped to this one file. Union merge is WRONG for code: it would
# silently concatenate both sides of a conflicting function and produce
# something that compiles and misbehaves. It is right only where the content is
# an unordered list of independent additions.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
